// L9, the ERROR half: a public top-level `var` with no annotation whose
// initializer is syntactically a constructor call of a private class.
//
// The verdict splits on whether there is an anchor to point at. Here there is one —
// the call `Slot()` — so the diagnostic can name it and the answer is an error.
// When the type is inferred through several steps the anchor is the compiler's
// guess, and this codebase's history is unambiguous about erroring on guesses (BUGS
// #56's over-erroring "traded one silent wrong answer for a batch of false
// rejections"), so that case WARNS instead. test/pass/leak_inferred_warns.sf covers
// the warning half.
private class Slot {
    var value: Int
    fun init() { this.value = 0 }
    fun get(): Int { return this.value }
}

var registry = Slot()

IO.println(registry.get())
